This repository is the BoardUI chat starter. It contains BoardUI source:
components, styles, tokens, utilities and the chat runtime. That source is
licensed to you under the BoardUI License, whose full text lives at

    https://www.boardui.com/license

The page is the licence and controls if anything here reads differently. This
file summarises it and adds one permission specific to this starter.

WHAT YOU CAN DO

- Build unlimited end products with it: websites, applications, internal
  tools, personal and commercial, including products you sell.
- Modify anything. Rewrite it, restyle it, delete half of it.
- Keep your copy of this starter, including your changes, in your own
  repository, public or private, as the codebase of a product you are
  building. This is the permission the Deploy button relies on.
- Hand an end product over to a client, with the BoardUI code inside it.

WHAT YOU CANNOT DO

- Redistribute the BoardUI source, or a recognisable derivative of it, as
  source code: sell it, give it away, sublicense it, or offer it onward as a
  template, starter kit, boilerplate, theme, block collection or course. Your
  public repository is fine as your product; it is not fine as a kit for
  other people.
- Use it to build anything that competes with BoardUI: a component library,
  UI kit, design system, template marketplace, theme or Figma kit offered to
  other people, paid or free.
- Build a tool that lets other people browse, preview, generate, export or
  customise the BoardUI source.
- Remove or obscure licence notices in the files that carry them.

The line is simple. Shipping products built with BoardUI is the point.
Shipping BoardUI itself, or a substitute for it, is not.

